  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1243 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nThe rest of the afternoon looks fairly quiet and cloudy as a\nmoisture-starved upper-level waves (currently lifting across the\nIA/MO border) traverses into the Lower Great Lakes. Suppose a\nsprinkle or two cannot be ruled out (roughly a 10% chance for\nrain at any given location). \n\nWednesday is shaping up to be unseasonably mild area-wide. High\ntemperatures are forecasted to reach the low to mid-70s \nduring the afternoon amidst breezy southwest winds (gusts up to\n25 mph, especially with northwestward extent). \n\nThe next notable shortwave impulse is expected to track well \nnorth across southern Canada Wednesday night. As an associated \nsurface low moves eastward across Ontario, a southwestward-\ntrailing cold front will push southward into our area by \nThursday. Although the strongest large-scale forcing will pass \nwell to the north, pooling low-level moisture (dew points in \nthe mid to upper 50s) along the frontal boundary could support \nisolated to widely scattered showers, particularly late \nWednesday night into Thursday. Consequently, we maintain low- \nend (20 to 40%) chances of precipitation during this period.\n\nTemperatures Thursday and Friday look to be stunted by extensive\ncloud cover and onshore winds. Have aggressively undercut NBM \nguidance to now feature highs generally in the mid 60s to around\n70 on Thursday to solidly in the 60s on Friday (more more in \nline with ensemble guidance). Some deterministic guidance \nsuggests highs may struggle to climb out of the 50s on Friday \nnear the Wisconsin state line and Lake Michigan shoreline. \n\nEnsemble guidance suggests a series of impulses will track from\nMexico east-northeastward into the Lower Great Lakes region \nduring the weekend, followed by a potentially more substantial \nsystem tracking slowly across the central U.S. next week. As a \nresult, there will be daily chances for rain from Saturday into \nnext week. Dry periods are still expected, so it will not be \nraining continuously throughout the weekend.\n\nKJB/Borchardt",
